course: dictionary
lesson: 8290
title: Rising: going up and growing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rising means going up, or getting higher. The words around it give you the clue. «Warm air is rising» means the air is moving upwards. «Sea levels are rising» means the sea is getting higher over time.
explain: Look at the word after rising. A rising sun is the sun coming up in the morning. A rising star is someone becoming more successful. Rising prices are prices that keep getting higher. Ask yourself: what is going up here, in height, in number or in strength?
explain: Sometimes rising is a noun, meaning a rebellion against rulers. It often names an event in history, like the Easter Rising in Ireland, and it may have a capital letter. The context tells you which meaning fits.
fact: Rising means going up, or getting higher.
fact: Rising can mean getting bigger in number, amount or strength, as in «rising prices».
fact: «The rising sun» is the sun coming up in the morning.
fact: A «rising star» is someone who is becoming more important or successful.
fact: A rising (noun) is a rebellion against rulers, such as the Easter Rising in Ireland.
exercise: «Some people take a second job because low pay or rising prices make one job not enough.» What does rising mean in «rising prices»? | Getting lower | Getting cleaner | *Getting higher | Getting shorter
exercise: «Warm air is rising.» What is the warm air doing? | Staying still | Turning cold | *Moving upwards | Falling to the ground
exercise: «The rising sun lit up the hills.» What is rising in this sentence? | *The sun, coming up in the morning | The hills, going down into the valley | The clouds, slowly drifting away | The lights in the village
test: «Rivers are rising after heavy rain.» What might happen next? | The water will disappear | *The water may flood the land | The rivers will freeze solid | The rain will stop at once
test: Mia says, «She is a rising star at school.» What does rising mean here? | Standing still | Hiding away | *Becoming more successful | Falling behind
exam: «The Easter Rising in Ireland changed history.» Which meaning of rising fits? | Going up in height | The sun coming up | *A rebellion against rulers | Growing in number
